    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: when a POST `/api/owners` request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the owner's response carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`, computed against `registrationDate`. Since the test reads back through `GET`, the birth date has to round-trip through the DB and the band be derived on the response.\n\nI kept the change as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing function:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (input) to `OwnerFields` and a read-only `ageBand` (output) to `Owner`. The DTOs are generated from this spec, so request binding and response serialization come for free.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` field with a plain getter/setter (each CC 1), so JPA persists it and MapStruct maps it.\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column (the profile the tests run under).\n4. **`AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-method helper holding all the band logic, so its complexity lives in a class of its own (no surrounding context).\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line delegating to `AgeBand.of(...)`. This adds the derivation to *every* response path (single, list, page) idiomatically, matching how the other derived fields (`locality`, `contactPreference`, `membershipLevel`) are computed \u2014 without touching any responder function.\n\nNo existing function bodies were modified; the only edits to existing methods were a one-line annotation on the mapper's abstract `toOwnerDto` and trivial accessors on the entity.",
